    "collapsible_tabs_i7rBwx": {
      "type": "collapsible-tabs",
      "blocks": {
        "question_bmJh66": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What Is Water Soluble CBD and CBN?",
            "answer": "<p>CBD (cannabidiol) and CBN (cannabinol) are cannabinoids — natural hemp compounds that interact with the body's endocannabinoid system (ECS), a regulatory network involved in sleep, stress response, memory, and immune health. A growing body of research suggests CBD may help with <a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4604171/\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">managing stress</span></a>, accessing <a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6326553/\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">deeper, more restorative sleep</span></a>, and easing <a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7023045/\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">minor aches and strains</span></a>, while CBN is best known as a sleep aid with some <a href=\"https://www.jneurosci.org/content/22/11/4720.full\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">pain-fighting properties</span></a>. You can learn more about <a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/blogs/blog/what-is-the-endocannabinoid-system\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">how the ECS works</span></a> on our <a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/blogs/blog\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">cannabis and hemp blog</span></a>.</p><p>Because cannabinoids are naturally oil-based, they don't mix with water on their own. <strong>Water soluble CBD</strong> is made by breaking <a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">CBD oil</span></a> into microscopic droplets that form an easily absorbed emulsion. Our proprietary process uses only certified organic sunflower lecithin — no dirty emulsifiers, synthetic ingredients, or contaminants — plus a nano electrolyte blend that embeds nanoclusters of water into the formulation to maximize absorption.</p>",
            "button_txt": "",
            "link": "",
            "onclick": false,
            "onclick_code": "",
            "info": ""
          }
        },
        "question_qmDymB": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Is Water Soluble CBD Better Than CBD Oil?",
            "answer": "<p>The effects are the same — the difference is delivery. Traditional <a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/collections/cbd-tinctures\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">CBD oil and tinctures</span></a> use a carrier oil like MCT, which floats on liquids and carries a natural hemp taste. A <strong>water-based CBD tincture</strong> dissolves cleanly into coffee, tea, smoothies, juices, soups, or a water bottle you sip throughout the day — making <strong>CBD water</strong> as easy to prepare as adding milk or lemon. Thanks to higher bioavailability, water soluble formulas are also faster acting than oil when taken sublingually or swallowed.</p><p>The main benefits of HempLucid's water soluble CBD and CBN:</p><ul><li>Convenience and portability</li><li>Easy, precise dosing</li><li>Quick onset — roughly five to ten minutes sublingually</li><li>Maximum versatility in food and beverages (our <a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/products/thc-free-cbd-isolate-terpenes-water-soluble\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">THC-free water soluble CBD</span></a> can even be vaped)</li></ul><p>Prefer a different format? We also offer <a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/collections/edible-cbd\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">CBD gummies</span></a>, <a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/collections/cbd-capsules\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">CBD capsules</span></a>, <a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/collections/delta-8\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">Delta-8</span></a>, and functional blends for <a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/products/functional-gummies-sleep-cbd-cbn-mushroom\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">sleep</span></a> and <a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/products/functional-gummies-stress-cbd-herb-mushroom\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">stress</span></a>. For drinkable THC, see our guide to <a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/blogs/blog/thc-drops-explained-a-guide-to-water-soluble-beverage-enhancers\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">water-soluble THC drops and beverage enhancers</span></a>.</p>",
            "button_txt": "",
            "link": "",
            "onclick": false,
            "onclick_code": "",
            "info": ""
          }
        },
        "question_KDgMmq": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Full Spectrum vs. Broad Spectrum vs. CBD Isolate",
            "answer": "<p><strong>Water soluble full spectrum CBD</strong> is the least processed option and contains the plant's full range of cannabinoids, including trace amounts of THC — not enough to get you high, but enough to qualify as the most \"natural\" choice and, in our case, USDA certified organic. Broad spectrum removes the THC but keeps other cannabinoids like CBC and CBN, while CBD isolate is the most rigorously processed, leaving pure CBD with no THC at all. At HempLucid, most of our products use <a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/products/organic-cbd-full-spectrum-hemp-seed-oil\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">full spectrum extracts</span></a>, alongside two isolate tinctures — one water soluble and one MCT oil — for those who prefer zero THC.<br/><br/></p>",
            "button_txt": "",
            "link": "",
            "onclick": false,
            "onclick_code": "",
